    Bug 2000453 - Add 'Recent Destinations' settings to General panel and support alphabetical sorting. r=aleca


    This patch introduces user-facing controls for the behavior of the 'Recent
    Destinations' submenu of the folder widget and implements the option to sort
    the listed folders alphabetically.

    Added a new 'Recent Destinations' section to the General panel. This
    includes a selection menu (menulist) to choose between 'By last used' (MRU) and
    'Alphabetically' sorting, and a numeric input to define the maximum number of
    recent folders displayed. As part of this, the default maximum limit was
    reduced from 25 to 10; because the list defaults to recency-based sorting,
    a shorter list significantly improves visual scannability.

    Updated the folder popup logic to respect the new
    `mail.folder_widget.recent_sort_order` integer preference.

    Integrated an `nsIObserver` in the folder widget backend. This ensures that any
    cached folder menus (such as the 'Move to' or 'Copy to' submenus) are
    automatically rebuilt after these preferences have changed.

    Added a browser test in browser_general.js to verify that UI changes correctly
    update the underlying preferences and that the menu reflects those changes.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D282889

